---
/**
 * /privacy — what the site collects, where it goes, and what we do not do
 * with it. Plain and specific, in the site's voice: every statement here
 * maps to a mechanism in this repo (AuditForm, api/, analytics.js).
 *
 * PROVISIONAL: drafted 2026-09-06 for Jadrin's review and possibly a
 * lawyer's. Two facts are not in the repo and are flagged in the copy's
 * comments: a retention period for audit requests, and a postal address.
 */
import '../styles/system.css';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';

const updated = 'September 6, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy | VIIS Partners"
	description="What viispartners.com collects when you request an audit or visit the site, where it is stored, who sees it, and how to have it deleted."
>
	<SiteHeader />

	<main id="main">
		<Section labelledby="privacy-heading">
			<Eyebrow class="kicker">Privacy</Eyebrow>
			<h1 id="privacy-heading" class="headline">What this site collects, and what we do with it.</h1>
			<p class="t-lead fg-2 measure sub">
				Short version: the audit form collects five things you type, we store them in our own
				account to run your audit and reply, analytics counts visits without identifying you, and
				nothing is sold or shared with anyone.
			</p>
			<p class="t-mono fg-3 updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

			<div class="prose measure">
				<h2>The audit form</h2>
				<p>
					When you request a free audit, the form sends us your name, your business name, your
					email address, your website address, and, if you add one, a one-line note. That is all
					it asks for, and every field is capped in length.
				</p>
				<p>
					Alongside those five fields we record the time of the request, a scrambled version of
					your device's network address, and your browser's identifying string. The network
					address is hashed before it is stored and the original is never kept; we use the hash
					only to stop one source from flooding the form.
				</p>
				<p>
					Two emails go out when a request is accepted: a confirmation to the address you gave,
					and a notification to us. Both contain what you typed and nothing else.
				</p>

				<h2>Where it is stored</h2>
				<p>
					Requests are written to a table in a Microsoft Azure storage account that belongs to
					VIIS. The emails are sent through Azure's email service from the same account. No
					third-party form tool, mailing service, or marketing platform sits in that path.
				</p>
				<p>
					The hosting platform, Microsoft Azure, keeps its own standard operational logs. Our own
					application logs contain no personal information: hostnames and hash prefixes only.
				</p>

				<h2>Who sees it</h2>
				<p>
					One person: Jadrin Garcia, the principal of VIIS. Your request is used to run the audit,
					write the report, and reply to you. It is not used for a newsletter, it is not added to
					any list, and it is never sold, rented, or shared with another business.
				</p>
				<p>
					We keep audit requests for as long as we need them to run the audit and follow up on
					it. Ask and we delete yours.
				</p>

				<h2>Analytics</h2>
				<p>
					The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and to record when an audit request is
					accepted, so we know whether the site is doing its job. It is configured with Google
					Signals and advertising personalization switched off, which means it does not build an
					advertising profile of you and does not share your visit with Google's ad products. The
					event that records an accepted request carries no form data. Google processes this
					traffic under its own terms, and your network address is not stored by it.
				</p>

				<h2>Cookies</h2>
				<p>
					The site sets no cookies of its own. Google Analytics sets its own first-party cookies
					to tell a returning visit from a new one. Blocking them in your browser does not affect
					the site or the form.
				</p>

				<h2>What we do not do</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>We do not sell, rent, trade, or share your details with anyone.</li>
					<li>We do not send marketing email. A request gets a confirmation and a reply, and that is all.</li>
					<li>We do not embed social media, advertising pixels, chat widgets, or any third-party script other than Google Analytics.</li>
					<li>We do not collect anything from you that the form does not show you.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Your choices</h2>
				<p>
					Email us and we will send you a copy of what we hold about you, correct it, or delete
					it. There is no form for this and no waiting period: it is a reply from a person.
				</p>

				<h2>Contact</h2>
				<p>VIIS, LLC (d/b/a VIIS Partners), San Antonio, Texas.</p>
				<p><a href="mailto:jgarcia@viispartners.com">jgarcia@viispartners.com</a></p>
			</div>
		</Section>
	</main>

	<SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
	.kicker {
		display: flex;
	}

	.headline {
		margin-top: var(--sp-5);
	}

	.sub {
		margin-top: var(--sp-5);
	}

	.updated {
		margin-top: var(--sp-5);
	}

	.prose {
		margin-top: var(--sp-8);
	}

	/* Sections within the policy: an h2 opens each, with a section's worth
	   of breath above it but the prose rhythm below. */
	.prose h2 {
		margin-top: var(--sp-8);
	}

	.prose h2:first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.prose h2 + * {
		margin-top: var(--sp-4);
	}

	.prose ul > li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: var(--sp-5);
	}

	.prose ul > li + li {
		margin-top: var(--sp-3);
	}

	/* The site's jade mark, on the item's first line. */
	.prose ul > li::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		top: calc((var(--text-body) * var(--lh-body) - 6px) / 2);
		width: 6px;
		height: 6px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--accent);
	}
</style>
